eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elI.ep Introductioneo ğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

        This is rather more a technical help than explanations of the 
   rules of the game (but one could wonder what is "technical" in this file).
  For the rules you should refer to the infos-menu (in the middle of the main
    menu of the game).  Don't expect to find help on the level editor here:
   there is a separate file available in the editor with the [hkF1hi] key.

                

eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elII.ep Command line parameterseo ğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

  You can use theses options when you run Heroes.

poho   hkGO!hi        Skip the introduction and start directly at the front menu
    hkDEFOPTIONShi Restore the default options (like keyboard defs,
                     volume, speed, etc...)
    hkDEFSCOREShi  Restore an empty highscores list
    hkDEFSAVEShi   Restore an empty savedgames list
    hkHLPhi        ô 
poho   hkHELPhi       ³ Start this help reader
    hkINFOhi       õ
poho   hkCDhi         Start the CD player
poho   hkINSTALLhi    ô Start the installation program to 
    hkCOPYhi       õ  copy Heroes on your hard drive.
    hkJOYOFFhi     Disable joystick
    hkORDERhi      Display an order form.
    hkMONOhi       Disable stereo sound
    hkNOSFXhi      Disable sound FX
    hkNODOUBLEFXhi Prevent from running rotozoom and mushroom at the same
               time (for slow computers).
poho   hkSETUPhi      Run the sound setup menu
    hkSWAPSIDEhi   Swap player-1 and player-2's views.
    hkWINhi        Use this option under windows95.

  For exemple, "hkheroes joyoff monohi" will start Heroes in mono and
  without joystick support.

eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elIII.ep System configuration eo ğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

        The recommended configuration for HEROES is:
                hnohi Pentium class CPU running at about 133MHz
                hnohi some 8Mb of RAM should be enough
                hnohi MS-DOS is the right OS for this game (see the next 
                    paragraph); you don't need EMM386.EXE nor HIMEM.SYS
                hnohi A sound card (Gravis UltraSound is better)                              


hm     This game, HEROES, was designed to be run under DOS, not Windows.
     We *tried* to make it runnable under Windows, so you could play
     HEROES there if you don't care about fluidity. If you own Windows
hm     you are strongly encouraged to run HEROES in "MSDOS mode" for best
hm     results.hi I (Pollux) don't have a high opinion of Windows95 and its
     makers but I won't go to the mat here, anyway this explains some
     sentences in the rest of this file :)

     Under Windows 95 you shall try to create a .PIF extension in order
     to run Heroes:
          - right clic on "Heroes.exe" and select "Properties"
          - At the top of the properties box, select "Screen"
          - Then check "Full-screen"
          - At the top of the properties box, select "Program"
          - Add "WIN" to the command line, like this:
                "X:\XXXXXX\HEROES.EXE WIN"
          - At the bottom, press the "Advanced..." button
          - In this "Advanced Program Settings" :
              [ ]  Uncheck "Prevent MS-DOS-based programs from detecting win"
              [ ]  Uncheck "Suggest MS-DOS mode as necessary"
     This was for running Heroes *in* windows. It is far better to run
     Heroes in MS-DOS mode. For this goal, in "Advanced Program Settings"
              [X]  Check "MS-DOS mode"
     and do NOT add "WIN" to the command line.


eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elIV.ep Extra-levels eoğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

     This version of Heroes provides a level editor. This allow you to
     build new levels (=extra-levels) and play them. Each extra-level is a
     single file located in the EXTRALVL subdirectory.  The CD version of
     Heroes should include a set of extra-levels (those we did not want
     to include in the game) that you will be able to modify and/or play.

     To run the editor, just select EDITOR in the main menu.  You may
     be prompted whether you want to create a new level or edit a existing
     one. Before creating a new level you will have to enter its dimension,
     type its name, and select the tiles set (=the world) it will use.
     (horinzontal and vertical wrappings are effective only with power of
     two dimensions).

     As it was said before, the level editor is explained in a separate
     help file. Just run the editor and press [F1] to see it.

     Playing extra-levels should be quite easy. The whole thing is handled
     by the EXTRAS screen of the options-menu. You first say whether you
     want to play standard levels, extra levels, or both; then you precise
     if you want to play with all extra levels or just a subset; and in this
     last case you will have to check each extra-level that should be
     included.

     Notice that you can play extra-levels only in round-oriented games
     (that is any mode but QUEST) where levels are randomly loaded.


eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elV.ep Installation and updates eoğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

     Installation of Heroes can be done by running 'HEROES INSTALL'. This
     asks you for a drive and a directory, and do the rest.

     I am going to explain how files are used in Heroes in case this
     installation fails.  In fact manualy copying HEROES.EXE before
     running it should work, even if there was some other files in the
     same directory before.  HEROES.EXE contains all the datas needed by
     the game to work (even highscores and savedgames, that you can
     reset with the DEF**** parameters - see paragraph II.).

     When you run Heroes, it creates some batch files for your comfort;
     under windows, it also create an icon. So you don't need to copy
     theses files.

     In the full version, you should additionaly copy the EXTRALVL
     subdirectory.

     Updates :
     Should we have to make a new version of Heroes (for a bug fix or an
     improvment) we would spread a small patch for update. This file would
     just have to be copied in Heroes' directory.


