eo-Ä-ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-=ğ elVII.ep Never Asked Questionseo ğ=ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ-Ä--

hmQ:he How do I play Heroes?
hkA:hi With hands. One of us tried to play it with feet, kneeled, with the screen
   behind him. But as he needed to turn his head over his shoulder to see the
   game he fell down, puting his face in an original Windoz95 box. He stil
   has a wonderful Mirco$oft logo printed on his forehead. But this virus
   seems to have proliferated and our friend is now told to have very few
   weeks left before he morphes into Gall Bites.
   Please, if you do not play Heroes with hands, ensure there is no Windoz
   tail around!

hmQ:he How do I disable these %œ@‡!$ samples that are played every two
he   minutes when I stand idle in the menu?
hkA:hi You can't! If you'd like to disable all the SFX, you can start
   Heroes with the command ligne argument hkNOSFXhi. Note that theses
   samples are never played when you are in the CREDITS screen, thus this
   would be a good place to record the musics for those who are interested
   in.  By the way, we made a CD with remix of the game's songs and more
   (in addition to the game itself), but as we are not selling the game,
   we won't sell the CD either.  Contact us if you are interested in
   getting a copy of this CD.

hmQ:he How can I hear Heroes?
hkA:hi Buy one of these amazing monotranscendental telescopic 256bits oversuround
   fullcolor ovenproof interface and plug it in a yellow bean, add custard
   and basilic, and put it all 3 minutes under microwaves. Keep it two days
   in the fridge before updating your computer (use the "Windoz new device
   autodestroy system" if you can't install it by yourself).

hmQ:he I can't use my joystick in Heores. What should I do?
hkA:hi First, ensure it is connected to your computer ;-), and verify its
   port is enabled (for example run MSD or try to play another game with it).
   Next, run Heroes (and ensure you do no use the hkJOYOFFhi argument! ;-), in
   the menu use your keyboard to select OPTIONS, then CONTROLS, and change
   the player INPUT of a player to joystick. You should now be able to
   navigate in the menus with your joystick. If not, there is a problem,
   please report the bug. You can't change joystick (i.e. unplugging the
   current for plugging another one) during the game, you have to restart
   Heroes. hkNOTE:hi Heroes assumes that your joystick is centered when the
   game loads, this avoid any tedious calibrating screen. If you don't
   let the stick centered during the load you will get wrong movements during
   the game.

hmQ:he What can I do if I find a bug in Heroes?
hkA:hi Kill it quickly so nobody else could see it (a chain saw will do the work).
   Try first to carve the screen, then, if the bugs is still alive, you can
   do your job on the CPU. Keep your computer plugged for fun!

hmQ:he The level-editor don't start, when I select EDITOR in the main menu
   nothing happens.
hkA:hi You probably don't have a mouse driver loaded. You need a mouse in
   order to use the editor. hkNOTE:hi EDITOR is available in the full
   version only (and replaces the <ORDER> item of the main menu).

hmQ:he The level-editor don't start, I get the config screen (where I can
he   select tiles, dimensions, etc...), but when I select >EDIT<, the game
he   hangs, or comes back to the main menu :(
hkA:hi This should not occur now... try to redo the same actions and write to
   Pollux if it still hangs. 

hmQ:he I need help about the level-editor.
hkA:hi Start it and press [F1] when your are editing a level.

